home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/bn254_poseidon2.cu`, lines 183-223\n   - **Purpose:** BN254 Poseidon2 variant of row hashing for Groth16-friendly proofs\n\n**Merkle Layer Compression Kernels:**\n\n4. **`poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel`**\n   - **File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu`, lines 153-177\n   - **Purpose:** Compresses adjacent pairs of digests with configurable stride for building upper Merkle layers\n   - **Called 25 times** per your profiling (231ms / 25 instances = 9.24ms/instance)\n\n5. **`bn254_adjacent_compress_layer_kernel`**\n   - **File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/bn254_poseidon2.cu`, lines 277-288\n   - **Purpose:** BN254 variant that compresses adjacent digest pairs (stride=1) for upper Merkle layers\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Rust FFI Bindings**\n\n**For BabyBear Poseidon2:**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs`, lines 5-42\n  - `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes` (extern declaration, line 6)\n  - `_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext` (line 14)\n  - `_poseidon2_strided_compress_layer` (line 22)\n  - `_poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer` (line 29)\n\n**Safe Rust wrappers:**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs`, lines 52-144\n  - `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes()` (line 52)\n  - `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext()` (line 81)\n  - `poseidon2_strided_compress_layer()` (line 108)\n  - `poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer()` (line 132)\n\n**For BN254:**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/bn254_merkle_tree.rs`, lines 63-83\n  - `_bn254_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes` (line 63)\n  - `_bn254_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext` (line 71)\n  - `_bn254_poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer` (line 79)\n\n---\n\n### 4. **What `calculate_zero_hash` Computes**\n\nThe kernel computes:\n1. **Row Hashing Phase** (lines 39-51 of merkle_tree.cu):\n   - For each row, absorbs all column values into a Poseidon2 sponge state\n   - Padding-free sponge with CELLS_RATE elements per permutation\n   - Outputs CELLS_OUT field elements (8 for BabyBear Poseidon2, 1 for BN254)\n\n2. **Tree Reduction Phase** (lines 53-71):\n   - Builds `log_rows_per_query` layers of Merkle tree in-place\n   - Binary tree with `2^log_rows_per_query` leaves (one per strided row)\n   - Uses shared memory for pairwise node compression\n   - Syncs between layers for correctness\n\n**Why 584 instances:**\n- The prover commits to multiple different matrices (main trace, cached traces, preprocessed data)\n- Each matrix gets its own Merkle tree\n- Query stride determines leaf count; `rows_per_query` determines tree height parameter `k`\n- 584 total invocations across all AIRs and matrices at APC 300 config\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Merkle Tree Construction Call Chain**\n\n**Entry Point (from prover):**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs`, lines 48-84\n  - **`stacked_commit()` function**\n  - Instrumented with `#[instrument(level = \"info\", skip_all)]`\n  - Responsible for: stacking traces → RS encoding → Merkle tree construction\n  - Line 71: `MerkleTreeGpu::<F, MH::Digest>::new_with_hash::<MH>()`\n\n**Merkle Tree Constructor (dispatch layer):**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs`, lines 99-172\n  - **`MerkleTreeGpu::<F, D>::new_generic_with_hash()`** (line 113)\n  - Instrumented with `#[instrument(name = \"merkle_tree\", skip_all)]` (line 104)\n  - Flow:\n    1. Line 126: Calculate `query_stride = height / rows_per_query`\n    2. Line 130-137: **Call `MH::compress_rows()`** → launches poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel\n    3. Line 142-160: Loop to build upper layers:\n       - Allocate digest_layers[i]\n       - Line 152: **Call `MH::compress_layer()`** → launches poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel (or adjacent for stride=1)\n    4. Line 163: Copy root to host memory\n\n**Hash Scheme Dispatch (routes to correct kernel):**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs`, lines 36-87\n  - **`GpuMerkleHash` trait** (line 36)\n  - `compress_rows()`, `compress_rows_ext()`, `compress_layer()` abstract methods\n  - **`Poseidon2MerkleHash` impl** (lines 118-148): uses BabyBear Poseidon2 kernels\n  - **`Bn254Poseidon2MerkleHash` impl** (lines 181-212): uses BN254 Poseidon2 kernels\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Trace Commitment Timing Span**\n\n**\"Trace Commit\" Phase:**\n- **Rust instrumentation point:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs`, lines 118-156\n  - Line 118: `let _main_commit_span = info_span!(\"prover.main_trace_commit\", phase = \"prover\").entered();`\n  - Line 119-125: Calls `self.device.commit(&traces)?`\n  - Line 156: `drop(_main_commit_span);` - timing ends **before** the constraint proof computation\n\n**This timing span INCLUDES:**\n1. Calling device.commit() which:\n   - Calls `stacked_commit()` (in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs:48`)\n   - Which includes:\n     - Stack traces (line 66)\n     - RS encoding (line 70)\n     - **Merkle tree construction** (line 71) ← **Where poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes is called**\n\n**So YES, the 107ms of `calculate_zero_hash` (poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes) is INSIDE the \"Trace Commit\" timing:**\n- Trace Commit: 197ms total\n- poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes: 107ms (54% of trace commit time)\n- poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_ext: ~0ms or included in above\n- merkle_tree_compress (layer reduction): 75ms (38% of trace commit time)\n- merkle_tree_init: 71ms (36% of trace commit time) - may be overlapped\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Data Flow: Traces → Merkle Roots**\n\n```\nCommitted Traces (on GPU device memory)\n    ↓\nstacked_commit() [cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs:48]\n    ├─ stack_traces() [line 66]\n    │  └─ Stack multiple traces into single matrix\n    ├─ rs_code_matrix() [line 70]\n    │  └─ Batch expand → bit-reverse → batch NTT → RS codewords\n    └─ MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash::<MH>() [line 71]\n       └─ new_generic_with_hash() [cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs:113]\n          ├─ compress_rows() [line 130]\n          │  └─ poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel [merkle_tree.cu:16]\n          │     └─ Hash each row → compute query_stride digests\n          └─ while loop [line 143]\n             └─ compress_layer() × log₂(rows_per_query) times\n                └─ poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel [merkle_tree.cu:153]\n                   └─ Pairwise compress digests → build tree up to root\n    ↓\nMerkle Root (digests computed, root copied to host)\n    ↓\nReturned to prover as StackedPcsDataGpu { layout, matrix, tree }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Key File Locations Summary**\n\n| Component | File Path | Key Lines |\n|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Row hash kernel** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` | 12-79 (BabyBear), 81-149 (ext) |\n| **Layer compress kernel** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` | 153-177 |\n| **BN254 row hash kernel** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/bn254_poseidon2.cu` | 183-223 |\n| **BN254 layer kernel** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/bn254_poseidon2.cu` | 277-288 |\n| **Rust FFI bindings** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs` | 5-42, 52-144 |\n| **Rust FFI (BN254)** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/bn254_merkle_tree.rs` | 56-92, 245-300 |\n| **Hash scheme dispatch** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs` | 36-212 |\n| **Merkle tree constructor** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` | 99-172 |\n| **Stacked commit** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` | 48-84 |\n| **Trace commit timing** | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs` | 118-156 |\n\