olation, polynomial aggregation, and challenge sampling—which takes about 36ms. If I could push all of that to the GPU, I'd eliminate that CPU bottleneck entirely.\n\nThe approach would be to use a GPU kernel for per-trace polynomial reconstruction with pre-computed transformation matrices, then do a weighted reduction across traces on the GPU, and finally copy just the aggregated polynomial back to the CPU. That way the CPU only handles the transcript observe and challenge sampling.\n\nThis is the optimization I'm going with. Let me formalize it and create a plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1875,"cache_read_input_tokens":180239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1875},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"3a3670a2-fdc8-4c02-b9a3-6249fb453455"}
