ompute iDFT** via `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` (line 156-160)\n      3. Apply coefficient adjustment (Lagrange interpolation factor)\n      4. Store in transform[i * input_size + j]\n  \n  - **Logup** (lines 174-193):\n    - Similar process but preserves dimension (size × size instead of (d-1)*skip_domain → output_size)\n\n- **Lines 308-325**: GPU-side extraction call\n  ```rust\n  _round0_extract_zerocheck_poly(\n      d_batch_ptr.add(w.zc_batch_offset),\n      sum_buffer.as_ptr(),        // evaluations on all cosets\n      tables.zc_transform.as_ptr(),\n      tables.zc_input_size,\n      tables.zc_output_size,\n  )\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## KEY INSIGHTS FOR OPTIMIZATION\n\n### **Current Stacked Reduction Round 0 Bottleneck**\n\n**CPU-side reconstruction takes ~36ms** at APC 300 because:\n\n1. **D2H transfer**: Block sums (3 × skip_domain elements) transferred from GPU per trace\n2. **iDFT per bucket**: Line 653 performs `dft.idft()` for each of 3 G evaluations\n3. **Transpose + DFT**: Lines 656-669 reshape and perform batch DFT\n4. **Pointwise multiply + iDFT**: Lines 672-680\n\n### **Adaptation Strategy (GPU-Side Extraction)**\n\nInstead of:\n- GPU → G0, G1, G2 on identity coset\n- D2H copy\n- CPU iDFT + multiply + iDFT\n\nCompute:\n1. **All cosets on GPU** in the kernel (like constraint Round 0) OR\n2. **Pre-compute transformation matrices** offline (like logup zerocheck) that encode:\n   - Transpose (implicit in index mapping)\n   - iDFT applied to G0, G1, G2\n   - Polynomial multiplication (E0*G0 + E1*G1 + E2*G2)\n   - Final iDFT for s_0 coefficients\n\n3. **Single GPU matrix-vector multiply kernel** writes directly to batch array\n\n### **Required Changes**\n\n1. Pre-compute 3 transformation matrices (one per G_i) during setup\n   - Encode: iDFT + E_i interpolation factors for n ≥ 0\n   - Separate matrices for each n < 0 bucket\n   \n2. Create CUDA kernel similar to `round0_extract_zerocheck_kernel` for stacked reduction\n   \n3. Launch on G