es the plan handle edge cases (empty buckets, variable l_skip)?\n\nReturn: Findings, Improvements, Assessment."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":209992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"1ba07c18-179e-49ea-a56e-815e5a439a1e"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a2171def350b98b19","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV2cjEaR1zKGBoe6AzNm2L","description":"Review optimization plan","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are reviewing an implementation plan for a GPU STARK prover optimization. Review this plan following the review guideline below. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\n## Files to read (in order):\n1. /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md — the review standard\n2. /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md — project context\n3. /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md — the task being planned\n4. /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction/plan.md — the plan to review\n\n## Additional context:\n\nAfter reading the plan, you MUST also read these source files to verify the plan against the actual code:\n- /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs (lines 481-686) — the current CPU reconstruction code\n- /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu — the existing CUDA kernels\n- /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs — the Rust FFI bindings\n\nKey measurements for validation:\n- Current STARK excl trace APC 300: 1110ms\n- Current Stacked Reduction APC 300: 74ms (out of 1110ms total)\n- The Stacked Reduction GPU kernels (block_sum + fold_ple) consume ~40ms of GPU time; the remaining ~34ms is CPU reconstruction + D2H sync + other overhead\n- l_skip is determined at runtime from the proving key parameters\n\nReview the plan critically:\n1. Is the transformation matrix construction mathematically correct?\n2. Are the claimed savings realistic given the measured bottleneck?\n3. Is the kernel design appropriate for the workload?\n4. Are there simpler alternatives that achieve the same goal?\n5. Does the plan handle edge cases (empty buckets, variable l_skip)?\n\nReturn: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.","uuid":"1931fd56-9410-4022-8909-d36dccbecf4d","session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7"}
