{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4YQxKQhS9HkizyAAHiwYZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction\n2\t\n3\tMove the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using pre-computed transformation matrices, matching the pattern successfully used in the constraint Round 0 GPU poly extraction (task gpu-round0-poly-extraction, which saved 47ms). The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT sequentially on the host, creating a CPU bottleneck that blocks the GPU pipeline. A GPU kernel can perform the equivalent computation as a matrix-vector multiply, eliminating intermediate D2H copies and parallelizing the reconstruction.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BV2cjEaR1zKGBoe6AzNm2L","session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"a6ed1058-a1c8-4ed1-a87a-de71e5a4dd9b","timestamp":"2026-04-16T05:23:32.461Z"}
