gs on a 74ms operation. That's pretty modest. I think I need to reconsider the whole approach and be more realistic about what's actually worth optimizing. Let me look at the bigger picture instead of getting stuck on this one component.\n\nLooking at the overall performance scaling, round 0 barely improves as APC increases from 0 to 300—it stays around 178-182ms. That's a per-AIR overhead that doesn't scale, which suggests there might be better targets elsewhere in the pipeline. the ratio. But that doesn't make sense—the goal is to improve APC 300 performance, not degrade APC 0. I'll go with the Stacked Reduction GPU NTT optimization instead. The gains are modest but concrete, and it's the most viable path forward at this point.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1814,"cache_read_input_tokens":220566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1814},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"e8aa2f08-7814-4f0c-a9d0-5646f0a801ab"}
