 Fp NTTs correct for base-field twiddles?\n2. Is the shared memory estimate correct? (4 × large_uni_domain × sizeof(FpExt) = 4 × 512 × 16 = 32KB — but the plan mentions processing Fp components sequentially, which changes memory needs)\n3. Are the 10 NTT operations per bucket realistic, and does the GPU kernel actually save time vs CPU?\n4. Does the `device_ntt::ntt_natural_to_bitrev` work correctly when called with l_skip=9 (large_uni_domain=512) using 512 threads?\n5. Is the active bucket detection via tracking n values correct?\n6. Is the Pre-DFT E approach (Step 5) adding CPU work that offsets the savings?\n\nReturn: Findings, Improvements, Assessment."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TvpUjpCExtn5Q8Q5HMqHC9","session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"c6ee4600-67da-44bb-9a22-364c71c42da6","timestamp":"2026-04-16T08:01:25.969Z"}
