{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012o2XQSZRaVaN8iPPoVLdrn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016voM3qTe6XH5E9PGjQjBy1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction\n\nMove the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline with `batch_ntt_small` and existing AoS/SoA conversion primitives. The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket D2H transfers (each syncing the stream), followed by serial iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT on the host. Moving this to GPU eliminates ~18 redundant stream syncs and ~60-80 CPU NTT operations, replacing them with batched GPU NTT calls that complete in microseconds.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":295,"cache_read_input_tokens":258229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":295},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fae41bbf-912e-42ee-9c72-17c79e3a14c7","uuid":"fbc3df9c-11f6-4153-b6fe-cf4c76d25c77"}
