onstruction.","+Move the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline with `batch_ntt_small` and existing AoS/SoA conversion primitives. The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket D2H transfers (each syncing the stream), followed by serial iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT on the host. Moving this to GPU eliminates ~18 redundant stream syncs and ~60-80 CPU NTT operations, replacing them with batched GPU NTT calls that complete in microseconds."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction\n\nMove the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using pre-computed transformation matrices, matching the pattern successfully used in the constraint Round 0 GPU poly extraction (task gpu-round0-poly-extraction, which saved 47ms). The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT sequentially on the host, creating a CPU bottleneck that blocks the GPU pipeline. A GPU kernel can perform the equivalent computation as a matrix-vector multiply, eliminating intermediate D2H copies and parallelizing the reconstruction.\n"}}
